abstract: "The Loop Test is a runnable AI Foundations study that distinguishes user-looping and content retrieval from path-dependent interaction organization. It compares an intact ordered interaction trajectory with content-preserving FACTS and SHUFFLED controls plus a BLANK baseline, and tests whether model-originated contributions remain consequential and persist without user reinforcement. A positive result supports path-dependent interaction organization under the tested conditions and does not by itself establish consciousness, subjective experience, personhood, or metaphysical identity."

